blem, we will use the relationships between the coefficients of the polynomial and its roots, as described by Vieta's formulas. Let's denote the roots of the equation \\(x^3 - 10x^2 + 55x - c = 0\\) by \\(r, s,\\) and \\(t\\).\n\nFrom Vieta's formulas, we know that for a cubic polynomial \\(ax^3 + bx^2 + cx + d = 0\\), the following relationships hold:\n1. The sum of the roots \\(r + s + t = -\\frac{b}{a}\\).\n2. The sum of the products of the roots taken two at a time \\(rs + rt + st = \\frac{c}{a}\\).\n3. The product of the roots \\(rst = -\\frac{d}{a}\\).\n\nIn our specific polynomial \\(x^3 - 10x^2 + 55x - c = 0\\), we have:\n- \\(a = 1\\)\n- \\(b = -10\\)\n- \\(c = 55\\)\n- \\(d = -c\\)\n\nUsing Vieta's formulas, we get:\n1. \\(r + s + t = 10\\)\n2. \\(rs + rt + st = 55\\)\n3. \\(rst = c\\)\n\nGiven that the product of two of the roots is \\(30\\), we can assume without loss of generality that \\(rs = 30\\). We need to find \\(c\\), which is the product of all three roots, \\(rst\\).\n\nFrom the second Vieta's formula, we have:\n\\[ rs + rt + st = 55 \\]\n\nSubstituting \\(rs = 30\\) into the equation, we get:\n\\[ 30 + rt + st = 55 \\]\n\\[ rt + st = 25 \\]\n\\[ t(r + s) = 25 \\]\n\nFrom the first Vieta's formula, we know:\n\\[ r + s + t = 10 \\]\n\nLet \\(u = r + s\\). Then we have:\n\\[ u + t = 10 \\]\n\\[ t = 10 - u \\]\n\nSubstituting \\(t = 10 - u\\) into \\(t(r + s) = 25\\), we get:\n\\[ (10 - u)u = 25 \\]\n\\[ 10u - u^2 = 25 \\]\n\\[ u^2 - 10u + 25 = 0 \\]\n\nThis is a quadratic equation in \\(u\\). Solving for \\(u\\), we get:\n\\[ u = \\frac{10 \\pm \\sqrt{10^2 - 4 \\cdot 1 \\cdot 25}}{2 \\cdot 1} \\]\n\\[ u = \\frac{10 \\pm \\sqrt{100 - 100}}{2} \\]\n\\[ u = \\frac{10 \\pm 0}{2} \\]\n\\[ u = 5 \\]\n\nThus, \\(r + s = 5\\) and \\(t = 10 - 5 = 5\\).\n\nNow, we can find \\(c\\):\n\\[ c = rst = 30 \\cdot 5 = 150 \\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\(c\\) is \\(\\boxed{150}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{150}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
